To start AmneziaVPN daemon at boot and stop it properly at shutdown,
make sure rc.local and rc.local_shutdown contain the following lines:

  /etc/rc.d/rc.local
  ==================
  # Start AmneziaVPN-service
  if [ -x @SYSCONFDIR@/rc.d/rc.amnezia ]; then
    @SYSCONFDIR@/rc.d/rc.amnezia start
  fi

  /etc/rc.d/rc.local_shutdown
  ===========================
  # Stop AmneziaVPN-service
  if [ -x @SYSCONFDIR@/rc.d/rc.amnezia ]; then
    @SYSCONFDIR@/rc.d/rc.amnezia stop
  fi

Make sure to replace @SYSCONFDIR@ with a value appropriate for your
_PREFIX, i. e. /etc or /usr/local/etc.
